.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt RSA_SIZE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm RSA_size ,
.Nm RSA_bits ,
.Nm RSA_security_bits
.Nd get RSA modulus size or security bits
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/rsa.h
.Ft int
.Fo RSA_bits
.Fa "const RSA *rsa"
.Fc
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft int
.Fo RSA_size
.Fa "const RSA *rsa"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo RSA_security_bits
.Fa "const RSA *rsa"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn RSA_bits
returns the number of significant bits.
.Pp
.Fa rsa
and
.Sy rsa-\(ran
must not be
.Dv NULL .
.Pp
The remaining functions described on this page are deprecated.
Applications should instead use
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_size 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_bits 3
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_security_bits 3 .
.Pp
.Fn RSA_size
returns the RSA modulus size in bytes.
It can be used to determine how much memory must be allocated for an RSA
encrypted value.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_security_bits
returns the number of security bits of the given
.Fa rsa
key.
See
.Xr BN_security_bits 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn RSA_bits
returns the number of bits in the key.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_size
returns the size of modulus in bytes.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_security_bits
returns the number of security bits.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr BN_num_bits 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn RSA_size
and
.Fn RSA_security_bits
functions were deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
The
.Fn RSA_bits
function was added in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
